        "raw_text_sha256": "24f6b6eb7075e7ef5d5285d6a7b091e67c1632db5432a4079813bf2908978fd9",
        "current_text_sha256": "16d4a06aa6895b235a9eaa21945a3d0a2c83232b9586112dfcc1c2666cedd54c"
      },
      "raw_text": "987. 求下列各式的值：а) $\\frac{1}{11-2\\sqrt{30}}-\\frac{1}{11+2\\sqrt{30}}$； б) $\\frac{5}{3+2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{5}{3-2\\sqrt{2}}$；в) $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}$； г) $\\frac{11+\\sqrt{21}}{11-\\sqrt{21}}+\\frac{11-\\sqrt{21}}{11+\\sqrt{21}}$。",
      "text": "987. 求下列各式的值：\na) $\\frac{1}{11-2\\sqrt{30}}-\\frac{1}{11+2\\sqrt{30}}$；\nb) $\\frac{5}{3+2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{5}{3-2\\sqrt{2}}$；\nc) $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}$；\nd) $\\frac{11+\\sqrt{21}}{11-\\sqrt{21}}+\\frac{11-\\sqrt{21}}{11+\\sqrt{21}}$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#2"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "$4\\sqrt{30}$",
          "derivation": [
            "$(11-2\\sqrt{30})(11+2\\sqrt{30})=121-120=1$.",
            "Combining the two fractions gives $\\frac{(11+2\\sqrt{30})-(11-2\\sqrt{30})}{1}=4\\sqrt{30}$."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression; no variable restrictions.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "$11+2\\sqrt{30}>0$ and $11-2\\sqrt{30}>0$, since both comparison quantities are positive and $121>120$; their product is 1.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{30}>0$."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The evaluated identity is unconditional for these fixed constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "$30$",
          "derivation": [
            "$(3+2\\sqrt{2})(3-2\\sqrt{2})=9-8=1$.",
            "The combined numerator is $5(3-2\\sqrt{2})+5(3+2\\sqrt{2})=30$, so the value is 30."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression; no variable restrictions.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "Both $3+2\\sqrt{2}$ and $3-2\\sqrt{2}$ are positive and nonzero, since $9>8$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{2}>0$."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The evaluated identity is unconditional for these fixed constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "source_label": "в",
          "answer": "$8$",
          "derivation": [
            "The common denominator is $(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})=5-3=2$.",
            "The numerator is $(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})^2+(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3})^2=2(5+3)=16$, giving $16/2=8$."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression; no variable restrictions.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "$\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}>0$ and $\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}>0$, since $5>3$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "Both principal roots are strictly positive."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The evaluated identity is unconditional for these fixed constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "source_label": "г",
          "answer": "$\\frac{71}{25}$",
          "derivation": [
            "The common denominator is $(11-\\sqrt{21})(11+\\sqrt{21})=121-21=100$.",
            "The numerator is $(11+\\sqrt{21})^2+(11-\\sqrt{21})^2=2(121+21)=284$, giving $284/100=71/25$."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression; no variable restrictions.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "Both $11-\\sqrt{21}$ and $11+\\sqrt{21}$ are positive and nonzero, since $121>21$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{21}>0$."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The evaluated identity is unconditional for these fixed constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
    {
      "number": "988",
      "source_number": "988",
      "source": {
        "raw_object_sha256": "5f959df4eb29957565b8db7e9975789eceb760a145acba1d71a373334e9b0a29",
        "current_object_sha256": "3365058a5605317e70eec812c2918669c595b16186133b619a42e2e03bb5b105",
        "raw_text_sha256": "ffa7487efa102430d4404fabf939e6e6d71d67a0e0821fac95506db7cbbb1df5",
        "current_text_sha256": "15613b2be1906cdd65b8bd47041f04564b33a4604c60d0e693cb856ad0cc6714"
      },
      "raw_text": "988. 证明下列等式成立：а) $\\frac{(2+\\sqrt{3})^2-1}{(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2}=\\sqrt{3}$； б) $\\frac{(3+\\sqrt{5})^2-4}{(\\sqrt{5}+1)^2}=\\sqrt{5}$。",
      "text": "988. 证明下列等式成立：\na) $\\frac{(2+\\sqrt{3})^2-1}{(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2}=\\sqrt{3}$；\nb) $\\frac{(3+\\sqrt{5})^2-4}{(\\sqrt{5}+1)^2}=\\sqrt{5}$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#3"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "The stated identity holds; the left side equals $\\sqrt{3}$.",
          "derivation": [
            "$(2+\\sqrt{3})^2-1=4+4\\sqrt{3}+3-1=6+4\\sqrt{3}$.",
            "$(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2=4+2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}(4+2\\sqrt{3})=6+4\\sqrt{3}$.",
            "The numerator is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the nonzero denominator, proving the identity."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "$(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2=4+2\\sqrt{3}>0$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{3}>0$; its square is 3."
          },
          "equality_cases": "Unconditional identity for the given constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "The stated identity holds; the left side equals $\\sqrt{5}$.",
          "derivation": [
            "$(3+\\sqrt{5})^2-4=9+6\\sqrt{5}+5-4=10+6\\sqrt{5}$.",
            "$(\\sqrt{5}+1)^2=6+2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}(6+2\\sqrt{5})=10+6\\sqrt{5}$.",
            "Dividing this equality by the positive denominator proves the identity."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "$(\\sqrt{5}+1)^2=6+2\\sqrt{5}>0$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{5}>0$; its square is 5."
          },
          "equality_cases": "Unconditional identity for the given constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
    {
      "number": "989",
      "source_number": "989",
      "source": {
        "raw_object_sha256": "d48fd579cf3af4deecbb58f96bff94a404d3244d8309a17b5be327c3961b8f35",
        "current_object_sha256": "22a650ac8702ede73c53c562155fedb6d4759aadd2d4b05078b0257a46649615",
        "raw_text_sha256": "c95985842b06bacc0ad600f955ab334e2a25918753ff56de2d71dbc19d4eaf59",
        "current_text_sha256": "1821aafd30a7fa3fcb057fe0a12e8861529e9cb197d0475ffdf7c91c550b5a08"
      },
      "raw_text": "989. 化简下列各式，并求它们的值：а) $\\frac{(\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b})^2-b}{\\sqrt{ab}+2b}$，设$a=5$，$b=2$；б) $\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})^2+4\\sqrt{xy}}{x+\\sqrt{xy}}$，设$x=0.4$，$y=0.6$。",
      "text": "989. 化简下列各式，并求它们的值：\na) $\\frac{(\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b})^2-b}{\\sqrt{ab}+2b}$，设$a=5$，$b=2$；\nb) $\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})^2+4\\sqrt{xy}}{x+\\sqrt{xy}}$，设$x=0.4$，$y=0.6$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#4"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "Simplification: $\\sqrt{a/b}$. At $a=5$, $b=2$: $\\sqrt{5/2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}$.",
          "simplified_expression": "$\\sqrt{a/b}$",
          "given_values": {"a": "5", "b": "2"},
          "exact_given_value": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}$",
          "derivation": [
            "The separate roots require $a\\geq0$ and $b\\geq0$. On this region $\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}$.",
            "Set $s=\\sqrt{a}\\geq0$, $t=\\sqrt{b}\\geq0$. The original numerator is $(s+t)^2-t^2=s(s+2t)$ and the denominator is $st+2t^2=t(s+2t)$.",
            "The denominator vanishes exactly when $t=0$, that is $b=0$; if $t>0$, then $s+2t>0$. On the original domain cancellation therefore gives $s/t=\\sqrt{a/b}$, including $a=0$.",
            "For the prescribed pair, $\\sqrt{a/b}=\\sqrt{5/2}=\\sqrt{10}/2$. Directly the numerator is $5+2\\sqrt{10}$ and denominator $\\sqrt{10}+4$; multiplying the latter by $\\sqrt{10}/2$ gives $5+2\\sqrt{10}$."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb R^2:a\\geq0,\\ b>0\\}$.",
            "stipulated": "Evaluate at $(a,b)=(5,2)$, which lies in the natural domain.",
            "denominators": "$\\sqrt{ab}+2b=\\sqrt{b}(\\sqrt{a}+2\\sqrt{b})>0$ on the natural domain. Both canceled factors are nonzero. The simplified expression must retain $a\\geq0,b>0$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt a\\geq0$, $\\sqrt b>0$, and $\\sqrt{a/b}\\geq0$."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The simplification is an identity throughout the natural domain; the value is zero exactly when $a=0$.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "Simplification: $1+\\sqrt{y/x}$. At $x=0.4$, $y=0.6$: $1+\\sqrt{3/2}=1+\\frac{\\sqrt6}{2}$.",
          "simplified_expression": "$1+\\sqrt{y/x}$",
          "given_values": {"x": "0.4 = 2/5", "y": "0.6 = 3/5"},
          "exact_given_value": "$1+\\frac{\\sqrt6}{2}$",
          "derivation": [
            "The separate roots require $x\\geq0,y\\geq0$. Set $u=\\sqrt x\\geq0$ and $v=\\sqrt y\\geq0$, so $\\sqrt{xy}=uv$.",
            "The numerator is $(u-v)^2+4uv=(u+v)^2$. The denominator is $u^2+uv=u(u+v)$.",
            "On the nonnegative quadrant the original denominator is zero exactly when $x=0$. For $x>0$, both $u>0$ and $u+v>0$, so cancellation yields $(u+v)/u=1+\\sqrt{y/x}$.",
            "Use the given terminating decimals exactly: $x=2/5$, $y=3/5$, so $y/x=3/2$ and the value is $1+\\sqrt6/2$.",
            "Direct substitution has numerator $1+2\\sqrt6/5=(5+2\\sqrt6)/5$ and denominator $(2+\\sqrt6)/5$. Since $(1+\\sqrt6/2)(2+\\sqrt6)=5+2\\sqrt6$, it gives the same exact value."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x>0,\\ y\\geq0\\}$.",
            "stipulated": "Evaluate at $(x,y)=(2/5,3/5)$, retaining the exact meanings of 0.4 and 0.6.",
            "denominators": "$x+\\sqrt{xy}=\\sqrt x(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)>0$ on the natural domain; both canceled factors are nonzero. No $x=0$ value may be restored after cancellation.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt x>0$, $\\sqrt y\\geq0$, $\\sqrt{y/x}\\geq0$."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The simplification holds on the entire natural domain; the simplified value is 1 exactly when $y=0$.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
    {
      "number": "990",
      "source_number": "990",
      "source": {
        "raw_object_sha256": "d5e36cd0817246f895a70e7bc3d8a71be9e4dbce4746a3d95c43dbd9999403be",
        "current_object_sha256": "ae3d3fc1390ad447b0f573b419201541596022623b2fae54eebe81efc58d982a",
        "raw_text_sha256": "4b1bc5b9eac660522e6575b7697596ce32de8f8be0656891f145018289dcbffb",
        "current_text_sha256": "3ac220a9a7f0870a9a520355e53d7e6bd5adc77f3f7c875180077f7a9162fec2"
      },
      "raw_text": "990. 化简：а) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a+\\sqrt{a^2-1}}{a-\\sqrt{a^2-1}}}$，其中$a\\geqslant1$； б) $\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sqrt{b^2+1}-b}{\\sqrt{b^2+1}+b}}$。",
      "text": "990. 化简：\na) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a+\\sqrt{a^2-1}}{a-\\sqrt{a^2-1}}}$，其中$a\\geqslant1$；\nb) $\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sqrt{b^2+1}-b}{\\sqrt{b^2+1}+b}}$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#5"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "Under the stated assumption $a\\geq1$, the result is $a+\\sqrt{a^2-1}$. On the full natural domain it is $|a+\\sqrt{a^2-1}|$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Put $r=\\sqrt{a^2-1}$. The inner root exists exactly when $|a|\\geq1$. Then $0\\leq r<|a|$ and $(a-r)(a+r)=a^2-r^2=1$.",
            "Neither factor is zero. For $a\\geq1$, both factors are positive; for $a\\leq-1$, both are negative. In either case the quotient is positive, so the outer principal root exists.",
            "Using the product 1, $\\frac{a+r}{a-r}=(a+r)^2$, hence its principal root is $|a+r|$.",
            "On the stipulated domain $a\\geq1$, $a+r>0$, giving $a+r$. On the other natural branch $a\\leq-1$, $a+r<0$, giving $-a-r$ instead; it must not be silently replaced by $a+r$ there."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.",
            "stipulated": "$[1,\\infty)$, as explicitly given in the statement.",
            "denominators": "$a-r\\neq0$ because $(a-r)(a+r)=1$. It is positive on the stipulated branch and negative on the other natural branch.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$r\\geq0$ and the outer square root is strictly positive; taking the root of $(a+r)^2$ requires the absolute value before using the stated sign."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The piecewise simplification is exact on both natural branches. On the stipulated domain the result is at least 1, with equality exactly at $a=1$; on the full natural domain equality to 1 occurs at $a=1$ or $a=-1$.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "$\\sqrt{b^2+1}-b$ for every real $b$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Set $s=\\sqrt{b^2+1}$. For every $b\\in\\mathbb R$, $s>|b|$, so both $s-b$ and $s+b$ are strictly positive.",
            "Their product is $(s-b)(s+b)=s^2-b^2=1$, hence $\\frac{s-b}{s+b}=(s-b)^2$.",
            "The principal square root is $|s-b|=s-b$, using its strict positivity; no restriction such as $b\\geq0$ is needed."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$b\\in\\mathbb R$.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumption; every real $b$ is allowed.",
            "denominators": "$\\sqrt{b^2+1}+b>|b|+b\\geq0$, with strict positivity from $s>|b|$.",
            "principal_root_signs": "The inner root is positive, the outer radicand is positive, and the resulting root $s-b$ is strictly positive."
          },
          "equality_cases": "The identity holds for every real $b$. The value is 1 exactly at $b=0$: $s-b=1$ implies $s=b+1>0$ and squaring gives $b=0$, which also directly yields 1.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
    {
      "number": "991",
      "source_number": "991",
      "source": {
        "raw_object_sha256": "33f6ea8c494f76983462fdc6574d53f24fa3df4de94f85cc3e1192e8ab670584",
        "current_object_sha256": "cd45756e238c924f782a8eaa3a0585ea2e8faf496323fc6c1bb5088d1f9eb7c8",
        "raw_text_sha256": "1e3eb573495db37ec20b0e1f84fa28023538c2ec53118462d4350e316902b612",
        "current_text_sha256": "960b8b34212b626b6628fdd81d96c4706445033a9cfd14e8965e00eb1c033c8e"
      },
      "raw_text": "991. 证明下列等式成立：а) $\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt{3}}=2\\sqrt{3}-1$；б) $\\sqrt{13+4\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt{3}}=11$。",
      "text": "991. 证明下列等式成立：\na) $\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt{3}}=2\\sqrt{3}-1$；\nb) $\\sqrt{13+4\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt{3}}=11$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#6"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "The stated identity holds: $\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt3}=2\\sqrt3-1$.",
          "derivation": [
            "$(2\\sqrt3-1)^2=12-4\\sqrt3+1=13-4\\sqrt3$.",
            "The candidate root is strictly positive: $2\\sqrt3>1$, because both quantities are nonnegative and $12>1$.",
            "The radicand is thus a strictly positive square. Its nonnegative principal root is $2\\sqrt3-1$, not the negative of this value."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Defined fixed real expression; $13-4\\sqrt3>0$.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "None.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$2\\sqrt3-1>0$ is established before identifying it as the principal root."
          },
          "equality_cases": "Unconditional identity for these constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "The stated identity holds; the product is $11$.",
          "derivation": [
            "$13+4\\sqrt3>0$, while $13-4\\sqrt3>0$ since $(4\\sqrt3)^2=48<169=13^2$ and both comparison quantities are positive.",
            "Both radicands are nonnegative, so their principal roots multiply to the principal root of their product.",
            "$\\sqrt{13+4\\sqrt3}\\sqrt{13-4\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt{169-48}=\\sqrt{121}=11$, the positive value."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Both fixed radicands are strictly positive, so the expression is real.",
            "stipulated": "No additional assumptions.",
            "denominators": "None.",
            "principal_root_signs": "Each factor is positive; the product and $\\sqrt{121}$ equal positive 11, never -11."
          },
          "equality_cases": "Unconditional identity for these constants.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
