        "current_text_sha256": "5b830802d688f79aaaf7bf6eb6df7602dcd0d4f3f101369bc30443598d035df1"
      },
      "raw_text": "992. 不查平方根表比较两个数的大小：а) $\\sqrt{7}$和$1+\\sqrt{3}$； б) $\\sqrt{19}$和$6-\\sqrt{3}$；в) $\\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{14}}{2}$和$\\sqrt{12}$； г) $2\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{3}$和$8$。",
      "text": "992. 不查平方根表比较两个数的大小：\na) $\\sqrt{7}$和$1+\\sqrt{3}$；\nb) $\\sqrt{19}$和$6-\\sqrt{3}$；\nc) $\\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{14}}{2}$和$\\sqrt{12}$；\nd) $2\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{3}$和$8$。",
      "pages": ["p0298#7", "p0299#1"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "$\\sqrt7<1+\\sqrt3$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Both numbers are positive, so comparing their squares preserves order.",
            "$(1+\\sqrt3)^2-7=4+2\\sqrt3-7=2\\sqrt3-3$.",
            "The positive quantities $2\\sqrt3$ and 3 satisfy $(2\\sqrt3)^2=12>9=3^2$, so the square difference is strictly positive and the asserted comparison follows. No root table or decimal approximation is used."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Both fixed real numbers are defined.",
            "stipulated": "Comparison without a square-root table.",
            "denominators": "None.",
            "principal_root_signs": "Both original numbers and both quantities used in the second squaring are positive."
          },
          "equality_cases": "No equality: the exact comparison $12>9$ is strict.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "$\\sqrt{19}>6-\\sqrt3$.",
          "derivation": [
            "$6-\\sqrt3>0$ since $36>3$; $\\sqrt{19}>0$ as well, so squares can be compared.",
            "$(6-\\sqrt3)^2=39-12\\sqrt3$. The difference $19-(39-12\\sqrt3)=12\\sqrt3-20=4(3\\sqrt3-5)$.",
            "Both $3\\sqrt3$ and 5 are positive, and their squares satisfy $27>25$. The difference is therefore positive, proving the strict comparison without a root table."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Both fixed real numbers are defined.",
            "stipulated": "Comparison without a square-root table.",
            "denominators": "None.",
            "principal_root_signs": "The subtractive expression $6-\\sqrt3$ is proved positive before squaring. The second comparison also uses positive quantities."
          },
          "equality_cases": "No equality: $27>25$ is strict.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "source_label": "в",
          "answer": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{14}}2<\\sqrt{12}$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Both original numbers are positive.",
            "$\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{14}}2\\right)^2=\\frac{24+2\\sqrt{140}}4=6+\\sqrt{35}$.",
            "The positive quantities $\\sqrt{35}$ and 6 satisfy $35<36$, hence $6+\\sqrt{35}<12=(\\sqrt{12})^2$. Positivity transfers the strict inequality back to the original numbers. This is entirely exact."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Both fixed real numbers are defined.",
            "stipulated": "Comparison without a square-root table.",
            "denominators": "The constant denominator 2 is nonzero.",
            "principal_root_signs": "All roots and both compared original numbers are strictly positive."
          },
          "equality_cases": "No equality: $35<36$ is strict.",
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "source_label": "г",
          "answer": "$2\\sqrt2+3\\sqrt3>8$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Both numbers are positive. The square of the first is $8+27+12\\sqrt6=35+12\\sqrt6$.",
            "Its square exceeds $8^2=64$ exactly when $12\\sqrt6>29$.",
            "Both sides of this last comparison are positive and their squares are $144\\cdot6=864>841=29^2$. Thus both comparisons are strict. No numerical root table is used."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "Both fixed real numbers are defined.",
            "stipulated": "Comparison without a square-root table.",
            "denominators": "None.",
            "principal_root_signs": "All quantities squared for the order comparisons are explicitly positive."
          },
          "equality_cases": "No equality: $864>841$ is strict.",
          "uncertainty": []
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": []
    },
