        "current_text_sha256": "1cb1b007379f61cc1fec438f37552acf8d8a91dcdbff4eb84fb3d44c6a0036bd"
      },
      "raw_text": "993. 证明：对于任何$a>0$和$b>0$，下列不等式成立：а) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}}\\geqslant\\frac{a+b}{2}$； б) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}}\\geqslant\\sqrt{ab}$；в) $\\sqrt{ab}\\geqslant\\frac{2ab}{a+b}$； г) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2}{b}}+\\sqrt{\\frac{b^2}{a}}\\geqslant\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b}$。",
      "text": "993. 证明：对于任何$a>0$和$b>0$，下列不等式成立：\na) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}}\\geqslant\\frac{a+b}{2}$；\nb) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}}\\geqslant\\sqrt{ab}$；\nc) $\\sqrt{ab}\\geqslant\\frac{2ab}{a+b}$；\nd) $\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2}{b}}+\\sqrt{\\frac{b^2}{a}}\\geqslant\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b}$。",
      "pages": ["p0299#2"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "The inequality holds for all stipulated $a,b>0$, with equality if and only if $a=b$.",
          "derivation": [
            "For $a,b>0$, both sides are positive. Their squared difference is $\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}-\\frac{(a+b)^2}{4}=\\frac{(a-b)^2}{4}\\geq0$.",
            "Because squaring is order-preserving on nonnegative numbers, this proves the requested inequality. Equality in the squared difference occurs exactly when $a=b$, giving the same equality condition in the original inequality.",
            "For completeness on the larger natural domain, the same square identity gives $\\sqrt{(a^2+b^2)/2}\\geq|a+b|/2\\geq(a+b)/2$. Equality there requires both $a=b$ and $a+b\\geq0$, namely $a=b\\geq0$."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$\\mathbb R^2$; the radicand $(a^2+b^2)/2$ is always nonnegative.",
            "stipulated": "$a>0,b>0$.",
            "denominators": "Only the nonzero constants 2 and 4 occur.",
            "principal_root_signs": "The left side is nonnegative on the natural domain and strictly positive on the stipulated domain. The stated positive-domain comparison uses a positive right side; the natural-domain extension retains the absolute value when taking its square root."
          },
          "equality_cases": {
            "stipulated": "$a=b>0$.",
            "natural": "$a=b\\geq0$."
          },
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "The inequality holds for all stipulated $a,b>0$, with equality if and only if $a=b$.",
          "derivation": [
            "Both sides are nonnegative whenever defined. The squared difference is $\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2}-ab=\\frac{(a-b)^2}{2}\\geq0$.",
            "Taking nonnegative principal roots preserves the comparison. Equality occurs if and only if $(a-b)^2=0$, or $a=b$.",
            "This proof also applies on the full natural domain $ab\\geq0$, including nonpositive pairs and zero boundary values."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb R^2:ab\\geq0\\}$.",
            "stipulated": "$a>0,b>0$.",
            "denominators": "Only the nonzero constant 2 occurs.",
            "principal_root_signs": "Both square roots are nonnegative on the natural domain and positive on the stipulated domain."
          },
          "equality_cases": {
            "stipulated": "$a=b>0$.",
            "natural": "$a=b$, for any real common value."
          },
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "source_label": "в",
          "answer": "The inequality holds for all stipulated $a,b>0$, with equality if and only if $a=b$.",
          "derivation": [
            "For $a,b>0$, both $\\sqrt{ab}>0$ and $a+b>0$. The difference of the two sides factors as $\\sqrt{ab}-\\frac{2ab}{a+b}=\\frac{\\sqrt{ab}(a+b-2\\sqrt{ab})}{a+b}=\\frac{\\sqrt{ab}(\\sqrt a-\\sqrt b)^2}{a+b}\\geq0$.",
            "The prefactor $\\sqrt{ab}/(a+b)$ is positive, so equality is equivalent to $\\sqrt a=\\sqrt b$, or $a=b$.",
            "On the full natural domain, $ab=0$ with $a+b\\neq0$ makes both sides zero. If $ab>0$ and $a+b>0$, both variables are positive and the preceding proof applies. If $ab>0$ and $a+b<0$, both variables are negative, making the left side positive and the right side negative, so the inequality is strict. These cases exhaust the natural domain."
          ],
          "domain": {
            "natural": "$\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb R^2:ab\\geq0,\\ a+b\\neq0\\}$.",
            "stipulated": "$a>0,b>0$.",
            "denominators": "$a+b\\neq0$ is an original restriction; on the stipulated domain it is strictly positive. Multiplication or division by it preserves order only on that positive branch.",
            "principal_root_signs": "$\\sqrt{ab}\\geq0$ on the natural domain and $\\sqrt{ab}>0$ on the stipulated domain; the individual roots used in factorization are used only for positive $a,b$."
          },
          "equality_cases": {
            "stipulated": "$a=b>0$.",
            "natural": "$ab=0$ with $a+b\\neq0$, or $a=b>0$."
          },
          "uncertainty": []
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "source_label": "г",
          "answer": "The inequality holds for every $a,b>0$, with equality if and only if $a=b$.",
          "derivation": [
            "The original individual roots require $a,b\\geq0$ and the radicand denominators require $a,b\\neq0$; thus the full natural domain is exactly $a,b>0$.",
            "On this domain $\\sqrt{a^2/b}=a/\\sqrt b$ and $\\sqrt{b^2/a}=b/\\sqrt a$, since $\\sqrt{a^2}=|a|=a$ and $\\sqrt{b^2}=|b|=b$.",
            "Let $u=\\sqrt a>0$, $v=\\sqrt b>0$. The difference between the left and right sides is $\\frac{u^2}{v}+\\frac{v^2}{u}-u-v=\\frac{u^3+v^3-u^2v-uv^2}{uv}=\\frac{(u+v)(u-v)^2}{uv}\\geq0$.",
            "Both $u+v$ and $uv$ are positive, so equality occurs exactly when $u=v$, equivalently $a=b$."
          ],
          "domain": {
